course: dictionary
lesson: 8788
title: Shamrock: a plant with a story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shamrock is a small green plant with three round leaves on each stem, a bit like clover. When you meet a new word, read the words around it for clues. Here the brackets tell you straight away what a shamrock looks like.
explain: «Pictures like a shamrock (a little clover with three leaves on one stem), or water as ice, liquid and steam, help explain the Trinity, but every picture falls short.» The brackets explain the word, so you do not need to stop and look it up. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A small plant with three leaves fits.
explain: Words can also belong to a story or a country. In Irish life and church, the story says Saint Patrick used a shamrock to explain the Holy Trinity: three leaves on one plant. Words like "the story says" tell you it is a story people tell, not something proved by science.
fact: A shamrock is a small green plant with three round leaves on each stem.
fact: A shamrock is a kind of clover, and it is a symbol of Ireland.
fact: On Saint Patrick's Day, people around the world wear shamrocks and green.
fact: The story says Saint Patrick used a shamrock to explain the Holy Trinity: three leaves, one plant.
fact: «Falls short» means is not quite as good as the real thing.
exercise: «Pictures like a shamrock (a little clover with three leaves on one stem)…» What is a shamrock like? | A red flower with five petals | *A little clover with three leaves on one stem | A grey stone | A tall tree with many branches
exercise: On Saint Patrick's Day, people around the world wear shamrocks and what colour? | Yellow | Red | Blue | *Green
exercise: The lesson says people «wear the shamrock». What does that suggest? | Leaving it on a bus | *Showing the shamrock as a symbol of Ireland | Painting it on a wall | Growing it in a garden
test: In nature lessons, a shamrock is a kind of what? | Tree | Fish | Rock | *Clover
test: What is the shamrock a symbol of? | Scotland | *Ireland | England | Wales
exam: In the story, why does Saint Patrick's shamrock have three leaves? | The plant is always broken | *To help explain the Holy Trinity: three leaves on one plant | It is a sign of rain | Because shamrocks are trees
